# Access and motion

Bake accessibility into every UI change. Do not ship structure, color, or interaction work without checking this list.

## Structure and names

- Keep one `h1` per page. Use landmarks that already exist: header, main, footer, nav.
- Label every control. Icon-only controls need `aria-label`.
- Do not remove the skip link or the route announcer.
- Dialogs (cart): `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal`, labelled title, focus trap (`useFocusTrap`), Escape, restore focus. Put the rest of the page `inert` while open. Wire `aria-expanded` / `aria-controls` on the opener.
- Custom listboxes (locale, currency): use `useListbox` (Arrow/Home/End, focus option on open, Escape restores trigger focus).

## Color and targets

- Text sits on `ink`, `muted`, or `on-soft`. Pastel fills use `text-on-soft`.
- Light-mode `--accent` / `--button` stay at AA contrast on paper (~`#7d6ba8`). White labels use `--on-button`. Do not lighten those tokens without rechecking contrast.
- Interactive targets stay at least 44px (`.btn`, `.icon-btn`, `.nav-link`, `.chip`, `.link-hit`, `.footer-link`). Inputs stay at 16px or larger.

## Forms, media, motion

- Forms: visible or `sr-only` labels; on validation use `aria-invalid`, `aria-describedby`, and `role="alert"` error text in every locale.
- Images that repeat a nearby title use an empty alt. Product / art pages use `products.<slug>.alt` (or equivalent descriptive alt).
- Motion is hover, a short page fade, and a slow hero drift. New animation and any start-at-`opacity: 0` state go inside `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`.
